urses in medicinal chemistry, pharmacology, pharmaceutics and the biomedical sciences. Research focus areas for the department include cancer research, drug delivery, genetics, eye diseases and neuropharmacology. The didactic courses, along with a research concentration in a specific area of pharmaceutical sciences, provide a strong foundation for academic, industry and other research careers.\nVisit Department\nView Requirements\nCost and Aid\nQuick Facts\nLocations\nBrookings Main Campus\nCredits\n60 Credit Plan\n90 Credit Plan\nEst. Time to Completion\n3-5 years\nStart Term\nFall\nIs it for you?\nThis program will be a good fit if you:\nHave an undergraduate or professional degree in pharmacy, chemistry, biology or a related field.\nHave a passion for laboratory research and scientific experimentation.\nWant to learn and work in a multidisciplinary research field.\nAre a good problem solver and analytical thinker.\nAppreciate working as part of a research team.\nJob Outlook\nBack to top\nCareer Opportunities\nExplore possible career opportunities with this degree:\nPharmaceutical industry\nAcademia\nRegulatory affairs\nNational research laboratories\nReady to take the next step?\nContact Our Department\nHemachand Tummala\nVisit Department\n605-688-4236\nHelpful Resources\nProgram Requirements\nPh.D. in Pharmaceutical Sciences\nDomestic Applicants\nInternational Applicants\nTuition and Funding\nGraduate Assistantships\nApply Now\nGraduate Admissions\nGraduate School\nYou may also be interested in...\nBiological Sciences (Ph.D.)\nGraduate\nNursing (Ph.D.)\nGraduate\nNutrition and Exercise Sciences (Ph.D.)\nGraduate\nPublic Health (MPH)\nGraduate\nBiochemistry (Ph.D.)\nGraduate\nChemistry (Ph.D.)\nGraduate\nBiological Sciences (Ph.D.) \u2013 Food Science Specialization\nGraduate\nBiological Sciences (Ph.D.) \u2013 Molecular Biology Specialization\nGraduate\nBiological Sciences (Ph.D.) \u2013 Microbiology Specialization\nGraduate\nPharmaceutical Sciences (B.S.)/Pharmacy (Pharm.D.)\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nVisit Us\nCome Meet Your Future\nMeet the people that will help shape your future and define your college experience! Learn more about your academic interests with some of our world-class faculty.\nApply Today\nPlan Your Visit\nRequest Info\nGet Directions\nGive to SDSU\nOffice Directory\nExplore\nAbout SDState\nAcademics\nAdmissions\nStudent Life\nResearch\nCommunity\nConnect\nAlumni\nAthletics\nBookstore\nEvent Calendar\nGiving\nLibrary\nNews\nFor Students\nD2L\nJacks Club Hub\nJacks Email\nMyJacks Card\nMyState\nSelf Service\nFor Faculty and Staff\nEmployment\nFaculty and Staff Directory\nInsideState\nMy Account\n\u00a9 2026 All Rights Reserved.\nEmergency\nEAO\nLegal\nMission\nPolicies\nReport It\nSDState Facebook\nSDState X.com\nSDState Youtube\nSDState Instagram\nSDState LinkedIn\nSearch\nFilter by Topic\nBlog Event News Profile Program\nAbout\nAbout Us\nUniversity Facts\nNews\nSandbox Login\nAwards and Rankings\nConsumer Information\nAccreditation\nAcademics\nColleges and Departments/Schools\nGeneral Education\nAcademic Calendar\nAcademic Catalog\nGraduate School\nHonors College\nLibrary\nAdmissions\nUndergraduate\nTransfer\nGraduate\nInternational Undergraduate\nOnline\nDual Credit\nPaying for College\nStudent Life\nHousing\nCampus Dining\nStudent Success\nStudent Experience\nUniversity Wellbeing\nParents and Families\nResearch\nEvents and Trainings\nFind Funding\nResearch Impact\nProposal Development\nResearch Support\nStudent Research Opportunities\nCommunity\nAttractions\nCamps and Conferences\nFamily Weekend\nSDState Experience\nSDSU Metro Center\nEvent Calendar\nSearch\nApply Today\nSDSTATE\nApply\nVisit\nDirectories\nDegree Finder\nFaculty and Staff\nOffice Directory\nBuildings Directory\nEvent Calendar\nCampus Map\nSDSTATE\nSearch\nVisit\nDegree Finder\nCampus Map\nSDSTATE\nApply Today", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.sdstate.edu/programs/graduate/pharmaceutical-sciences-phd#main-content"], ["A